<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="be0ad57e">&lt;h5&gt;
    Control the interview
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        As the interviewer, guide the interview and maintain focus on the objectives, but do not dominate the discussion
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To maintain appropriate control, avoid tangent conversations unrelated to the objectives
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Encourage open discussion as needed to expand on questions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Construct questions as needed to direct the interviewee to the desired information
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;
    Manage your interactions
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Maintain eye contact when asking questions and use active listening skills when the interviewee is responding
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Be respectful by allowing the interviewee to answer questions completely and do not interrupt
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Do not finish the interviewee’s sentences or make conclusions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Engage in the response and be an empathetic listener
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Allow a few moments of silence each time the interviewee stops talking
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Do not confront or challenge the interviewee
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Summarize key points made by the interviewee to confirm understanding of the response
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
