<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="efced4dd">&lt;h5&gt;
    Introduce team members
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        During the first interview, introduce yourself, other team members, EY and if appropriate, your title/role on the
        engagement
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Extend a culturally appropriate greeting, such as a handshake or bow
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Thank the interviewee for taking time to meet with you
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;
    Discuss interview length
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Advise the interviewee of the approximate amount of time the interview will take, normally no longer than an hour
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Verify that the interviewee has the approximate amount of time available or set a follow-up meeting to discuss the
        questions
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;
    Communicate objectives
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reconfirm the objectives of the interview with the interviewee
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Explain the meeting agenda
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Explain why the interviewee is the appropriate person to discuss these objectives
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Encourage open discussion
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Set the tone of the interview
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
