<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="3a42985a"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="6b8d28a7">&lt;h5&gt;
    &amp;nbsp;Ask interview questions
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Interview questions should be planned in advance of the meeting, to be sure that key objectives of the interview
        are adequately covered
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Begin with broad, open-ended questions (e.g., &quot;Tell me how the process works&quot;), and progress to specific directed
        questions (e.g., “How do you control the performance output from “xyz&quot;?&quot;) as the interview progresses
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Always begin with open-ended questions, such as &quot;Tell me how the process works&quot;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Depending on the interviewee’s response, ask additional open-ended questions until a good overview of the topic is
        obtained
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Then ask directed follow-up questions based on responses to the open-ended questions, to obtain the necessary
        details
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Avoid negative questions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Ask one question at a time and avoid asking multiple questions simultaneously
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;
    Take notes
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        For interviews with senior stakeholders and key process owners, it is advised that they be conducted by a team of
        two. One EY person is designated as the interviewer and the second EY person as scribe. This allows for a more
        robust record of events to be recorded and also to facilitate total understanding by the engagement team where
        complex activities and processes may be relayed.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Utilize the interview template and begin each interview on a new template
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Only take notes on a computer during an interview if the client does not object
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document the date, time and names of the individuals present during the interview
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Obtain all relevant contact information from the interviewee such as phone number and email address
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document the questions asked and interviewee’s responses with as much detail as possible while listening
        effectively
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        At the conclusion of the interview, revisit the key discussion points with the interviewee to confirm
        understanding. Make corrections to your notes as needed.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Transfer the notes to an electronic format as quickly as possible (same day preferred).
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
