<attribute name="name" nodeId="3a114186">Close and follow-up</attribute>
<attribute name="guid" nodeId="814f7eb4">_9HZZQEFkEeWKFM6svr2f9g</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="69fc681b">Close and follow-up</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="9dc9c0dc"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="9b705720">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="1d0981b0"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="84364f7a">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="dc1f5447"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="6a20baf4">&lt;ul class=&quot;noindent&quot;&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Closing an interview can be as critical as opening an interview when building client relationships, do not end an
        interview abruptly or at a critical point
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Ask the interviewee if there is anything else that should be discussed or if there are any important issues to
        expand on
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Thank the interviewee again for his or her time and cooperation
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Inform the interviewee that you might have follow-up questions or need additional assistance in the future and
        verify that you have the correct information
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Give the interviewee your contact details and invite the interviewee to contact you if there is something that was
        not discussed or there are other details relevant to the topic
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
